s__Strategy\n\n### ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst\ntype: ns__Decision\nXena: 'Every engagement starts with a diagnostic phase. Never propose solutions before understanding the system.' Two weeks, $5K, 8+ stakeholder interviews.\nDiagnostic First Methodology\nunder: ns__Strategy\n\n### ns__Actor_XenaGithubber\ntype: ns__Actor\nIndependent consultant specializing in knowledge mapping and organizational diagnostics.\nXena Githubber\n\n\n### Actor_XenaExpertgh — Xena ExpertGH\ntype: Actor\nwitnessed: 20261012\nXena ExpertGH\n\n(Actor_XenaExpertgh expanded as its own root — 1 children: each is rendered here or one door away; absence under this node is signal only after its doors.)\n\nTranscript — 1 statements in order; statement _<N> is ^Expr_20261012_2_SampleMemoryPhase2DeriveIdE2E_hd784eaed1223_<N>\n\n#### Sample Memory Phase 2 — Derive Id E2E · _1–_1\n_1 Xena ExpertGH: Reproduces the missing-id failure pattern from prod (## level heading, no id field). Must not crash; must produce a valid slug.\n\n# Coverage — under Actor_XenaExpertgh\n\nUnplaced (1): statements no position holds; ^Actor_XenaExpertgh::Unplaced holds them all.\n\n# Doors — Actor_XenaExpertgh's axes\n\n[ ^Actor_XenaExpertgh::Unplaced — 1 statements ]\nEach door expands to its complete axis, grouped again when it is long.\n\n\nserved: ^Actor_XenaExpertgh, ^Expr_20261012_2_SampleMemoryPhase2DeriveIdE2E_hd784eaed1223_1\n(pass this list back as `have` on your next expand — content you already hold is then returned as a bare ^pointer, never re-sent)","positions":"","pin":"96ab958342ea7969812fa1628f6921908457533b","positions_consult":"{\"positions\":[]}","context_bytes":3869},"live_run_id":"4eece11e0680","at":"2026-10-12T10:33:34Z"}
